title The wait that read as a fault
prompt Keaton: besides incense and grass, all ships cores need either fixing or conflict resolving or updating i.e. re-arming -- then, mid-round, a correction from the pane he was reading.
think I read the fleet before touching it: fleet_rearm.sh over all eight trees, then ps, then tmux capture-pane on every window. The panes were the reading that mattered. Six ships were at a shell prompt, each ending with the same four lines -- three laps died in under ten seconds, this is an invocation fault, try agent-jail by hand. diffuser 07:21:52, pheromone 07:21:44, petrichor 07:21:37, copal 07:26:00, grass 07:28:47. The session limit reset at 07:30.
think So the ships did not fail. They waited three times, were told waiting was a fault, and stopped nine minutes early. Only bakery lived, and only because its quickfail counter had not reached three when the clock turned -- which also corrects Keaton's read: the pane still running is bakery, and grass's window shows its loop ended at 07:28:47.
think Two ships needed more than a relaunch. pheromone carried one finished signed commit its lap never sent (14ab16d19, GREEN on 131 guards); patchouli stood 17 behind with an expired OAuth session, and a hand had typed the loop with no seat argument, which resolved to incense and refused.
think I pushed pheromone's commit -- and that is my own red. I did not run reds_spine_derive first, and pheromone's row had renumbered locally to %467 while a peer published its own %467 at 20260906.053014. My push froze a double-booking into the anointed spine. Repaired by moving the later stamp to %470, per the law's own worked repair, and because the fold shelf and the fold recital both spell rows-467-468 in a closed record.
think Then the instrument that answers a dark fleet: fleet_rearm.sh reads the roster for its report and spelled six seat names by hand for its paste. bakery, diffuser, grass, copal and patchouli each printed RELAUNCH: followed by nothing. Five of eight live ships, and the witness never noticed because every assertion in it named a seat the stale list happened to carry.
obs THE ELDER RULE WAS RIGHT AND ITS REASONING WAS TOO WIDE. %414's comment reads: the fault is upstream of the agent and no number of retries will reach past it. True of an ai-jail flag refusal. A spent session limit is upstream of the agent too, and clears on a clock. Same shape, opposite answer: stop and fetch a person, against hold and try again. The repair is an ORDER -- ask the limit question before the elapsed question, since a limit refusal returns instantly and would otherwise be classified by time alone.
obs A WITNESS THAT NAMES ITS SUBJECTS BY NAME CANNOT SEE A LIST GO STALE. Every leg of fleet_rearm_witness.rish passed while five ships got a blank paste, because each leg named silence or mind. The new leg plants copal -- a live seat the elder list never knew -- and beneath it a shape-based sweep counts empty pastes across the whole card rather than trusting one name.
obs TWO ROSTER GUARDS WERE RED BEFORE I ARRIVED, ON ONE BROKEN LINK. readme_reach and reds_fold both refused because construction/CHECKPOINTS.md pointed at archive/REDS-a-command-string-is-not-a-process-rows-462.md and the shelf on disk is REDS-what-the-instrument-was-looking-at-rows-462.md. One repointed link took both green, and the roster from roster_broken to ok.
